7th ascension so far (wiz, val, kni, wiz, sam, tou).

First !wish and !polyObj ascension for me.

Notes: no magicmarkers, no special helmets apart from 2 [oOA, no sleep
resistance before Vlad's tower (orange dragon + "MB).

Early game

A bonesfile with BoH and luckstone was. And the blessed rustproof Excalibur
one of my late knights had left. And the Sting. Of course, I didn't use
either of them, being a chaotic orc.  One of the two (or three?) bonefiles
also had 2 ?geno which resulted me having an extra 100 HPs.

Got Cleaver from one of the many altars in the dungeon. Somewhere before
the Medusa level I got scales from a silver dragon and found a [MR. After
this I did the quest. Once I was down to ~5 HP but a prayer took care of that.

When I got to the Medusa, a nymph stole the cloak and died over
water. Didn't find the stolen goods with freeze'n'dig-method. This also
resulted me to lose !polyself when I got polyed into a silver dragon by a
trap in the Mines.

I didn't find any other sources of MR, so I had to do the Castle without
MR. Only drawback was that a master lich cursed my cleaver, so I had to go
through several fountains to uncurse it. I tried to pray, but Set got angry
at me. It was a time for a sacfest to mollify him and get a decent
onehanded weapon. Sacfest gave me Ogresmasher and Strombringer, which was
my main weapon for the rest of the game. I also practised #twoweaponing.

One of the four dragons in the castle was gray and left scales, so I change
to gray dragon scale mail and "oR.

Until finding Fort Ludious, I had only one point of protection from
Set. There was a crossaligned temple in the Minetown and somewhere between
Oracle and Medusa. The spare temple was nice to have, since the priest in
the Minetown got killed accidentally by me applying firehorn several times
from the outside of the temple. I also tested almost all of the helmets,
cloaks, high boots and cloves from the Fort. The best items were blessed +3
helmet and dented pot.

In the Valley two nalfeshnees summoned Juiblex and Yeenoghu at the same
time, but Juiblex didn't even try to swallow me. Both were gone fairly
quickly.

Gehennom was quite uneventful, although Vlad's tower had an Archon, which
was a surprise, because I was only level 16 at the time. "Radiant sir,
radiant!"

Found speed boots and a +1 [oDisplacement in the Sanctum.

Rodney's first reincarnation came after me only after killing the high
priest of Moloch. 20 ?tele, teleportitis and intrinsic TC helped the way
back up.

There was an another Archon when I got back to dlvl 1. It had looted my
stash, and was wielding ogresmasher. Doesn't Archons respect E-word? Well,
apparently no..

Hmm, only one ?oGD, no magicmarkers. Well, we'll just have to
manage. Almost killed meself by eating a C-ration while standing on the
stairs and satiated: "You're finally finished". Stupid me..


Plane of Earth: killed Rodney and zapped /oDigs until found the portal.

Plane of Air: #invoke the Heart of Ahriman to levitate, quaff a !oConf and
read the only ?oGD. The portal was exactly on the other side of the
level. Air elementals swallowed me couple of times, but I managed to dodge
the quite well. Dropped the /oDigs inside a steam vortex.

Plane of Fire: just hack'n'slashed around. Yet another Archon! No
summoning, no problems. Got a message of someone disappearing a couple of
times and after spending maybe 500 turns on the Plane found the portal.

Plane of water: "You levitate over a bubble" or something like that. (>) to
get down, and floated around until the portal got me.

Astral Plane: Guardian angel. Stormbringer sliced him, but he stayed
tame. Famine on the right, Death on the center and Pestilence on the
left. Famine is the easiest IMO, so right it is. /oDeath for the Famine and
the altar was Set's!

Since I had played petless after the early game, I had left the magic
whistle somewhere, so no go for the Guardian Angel..


